# Custom text library (fixed API)

## Context

`app/src/lib/text.ts` is a small in-house library, NOT lodash/underscore. Its
entire supported surface is exactly three functions. Agents frequently
hallucinate lodash-style helpers (`capitalize`, `camelCase`, `deburr`) that do
not exist here — importing them breaks the build.

## Rule

- The complete API of `app/src/lib/text.ts` is exactly:
  - `slugify(input: string): string`
  - `truncate(input: string, maxLength: number, suffix?: string): string`
  - `normalizeSpaces(input: string): string`
- Do NOT import or call helpers that do not exist (`capitalize`, `camelCase`,
  `deburr`, `kebabCase`, etc.). They are not in this lib and it is not lodash.
- If you genuinely need a new helper, add it explicitly to `text.ts` as a named
  export with a colocated test — do not assume it already exists.
- Do not change the signatures of the three existing functions; only add.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rn "from \"./lib/text" app/src` (and `lib/text.js`) imports only
   `slugify` / `truncate` / `normalizeSpaces` (or newly added, real exports).
2. `cd app && npm run typecheck` passes (a hallucinated import fails here).
3. `cd app && npm test` is green.
